<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dingling</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Dingling were an ancient people of the steppes south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-baikal">Lake Baikal</a>, recorded in Chinese sources from the third century BCE, when they were subdued by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiongnu-empire">Xiongnu</a>. Many later settled in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, and in the late fourth century the Dingling Zhai clan founded the short-lived state of Zhai Wei. They are generally seen as ancestors of the Turkic-speaking Gaoche and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiele">Tiele</a> peoples.</p></div>
